                <pb facs="1141" n="1131" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.9531/7–749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hawthrone</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-07T21:00:00-04:00">July 7, 1949—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>184. Dept assumes ConGen has protested to local Aliens Affairs Office re order
                    vacate premises nr 1 Kwangsi Road (urtel 307, July 2). US Govt has only
                    provisional title this property. However ConGen should inform Commie auths
                    property is regarded as US Govt owned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
